"- Inner Bottle Wall\n    - Attribute 1 Type - smooth, curved inner surface of a glass container\n    - Attribute 2 Color - dark, almost black with subtle amber or coppery reflections along the rim\n    - Attribute 3 Size - circular, with a diameter that appears consistent with a standard bottle neck; inner wall depth not measurable from image\n    - Attribute 4 Material - glass\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - transparent glass with slight surface texture or residue, possibly from manufacturing or liquid contact\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - one continuous inner wall surface\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - forms the inner boundary of the bottle neck, surrounding the central aperture\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - concentrically aligned with the central aperture, facing inward toward the center\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - seamlessly connected to the outer glass rim and the central aperture, forming a continuous cylindrical structure\n\n- Glass Rim\n    - Attribute 1 Type - thick, rounded, glossy edge of the bottle neck\n    - Attribute 2 Color - dark brown or black with golden-orange reflective highlights due to light refraction\n    - Attribute 3 Size - circular, with a width that appears uniform around the circumference; outer edge slightly thicker than inner edge\n    - Attribute 4 Material - glass\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - glass with slight imperfections or residue, possibly from manufacturing or liquid contact\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - one continuous rim encircling the bottle neck\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - positioned at the outermost edge of the bottle neck, surrounding the inner bottle wall\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - horizontal, circular, facing outward from the bottle\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - fused with the inner bottle wall and the central aperture, forming a continuous boundary\n\n- Bottle Neck Opening\n    - Attribute 1 Type - circular opening at the top of the bottle neck\n   